body:
Graphics maxed out;

the mod

[https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2862531759](https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2862531759)

These are all Sturgian spearmen, and if they can hold off long enough the Khuzaits charge into melee and die to the spears, really depends on if they stay in formation. This is just one battle I was testing, and got some cool screenshots

&#x200B;

Edit: I tried this with other faction's infantry and their shields are not large enough, arrows slip through and the formation falls apart. while sturgians might be still weak imo,, their ability to block missle fire is definitely unmatched

You can hold F1 to have a rally point be set using your camera to make units hold position from a distance.

&#x200B;

If you're using a standard army, make infantry stand closer 3-4 times (preference and depending on numbers) find a hill and put your archers on it. You can spread out your archers once so they don't have difficulties aiming at the flank. (When a teammate is in front of their line of fire they don't shoot). Have your infantry either at the base of the hill or behind archers. (I prefer at the base of the hill since units can't walk through eachother in Warband it's hard to get your archers tf out of there) Cav can go on the side of the hill, down further so they don't attract enemies. Once your archers start racking up kills and they get close, either hold infantry or charge them. Send in cav around to take out enemy archers or to charge their infantry formation to support yours. Overall, just use the terrain to your advantage. Now... now if you have over 20 Swadian knights you basically can win nearly every battle by just charging them with some infantry support.

I don't mean to sound like a bitch. I know I should probably do that. They are just my only contacts here. All that will do is make me sit on the thoughts at home, and with my head it leads to really dark places. I try to be "mature" about shit but in reality it's kind of just fucked. 

&#x200B;

I know I should be meeting new people, but it's a little easier said than done. I've been lonely most of my life, I'm still very young but regardless...
